  "provider_query": "Find the public X status from OpenAI that announces GPT-4",
  "answer": "The official OpenAI account post that announced GPT-4 is from March 14, 2023.\n\n1. **OpenAI (@OpenAI)** — Mar 14, 2023, 17:00 UTC  \n   “Announcing GPT-4, a large multimodal model, with our best-ever results on capabilities and alignment: https://openai.com/product/gpt-4”  \n   https://x.com/OpenAI/status/1635687373060317185  \n   ~59.7k likes, ~16k reposts. Includes video. [web:0]\n\nRelated same-day posts from OpenAI leadership (not the company account):\n\n2. **Greg Brockman (@gdb)** — Mar 14, 2023, 17:00 UTC  \n   “We’re releasing GPT-4 — a large multimodal model (image & text in, text out)…”  \n   https://x.com/gdb/status/1635687252616679426 [web:4]\n\n3. **Sam Altman (@sama)** — Mar 14, 2023, 17:02 UTC  \n   “here is GPT-4, our most capable and aligned model yet. it is available today in our API (with a waitlist) and in ChatGPT+.”  \n   https://x.com/sama/status/1635687853324902401 [web:19]\n\n4. **Peter Welinder (@npew)** — Mar 14, 2023, 17:01 UTC  \n   “GPT-4 is here: our smartest and most reliable model yet!”  \n   https://x.com/npew/status/1635687624047489024 [web:9]\n\n5. **Mira Murati (@miramurati)** — Mar 14, 2023, 17:03 UTC  \n   “Unveiling GPT-4 — our large multimodal model…”  \n   https://x.com/miramurati/status/1635688069692293121 [web:1]\n\nThe company account post in (1) is the public OpenAI status that announces GPT-4.",
